Hello, this assembler was made by Doron Michal.
Before you begin checking the assembler, I would like to explain a few things:

1. the assembler keeps track of any errors by using a pointer to a struct called "ProgramState".
for any function that can result in an error, the pointer to the program state will be passed to it in the parameters,
and if the function finds any errors, it will set the state to an error, and the next time the state will be checked,
the error will be handled. you can read more about it in the utils.

2. in every test folder you will find another ReadMe file. the file will quickly explain what the folder is testing.
You can also check how the assembler handles multiple files at once by calling the assembler with the files you want to test.

Last thing, I would be glad if you wrote any mistakes you found in my assembler inside the notes file.
it is right next to this file. Goodbye :)

